// Chapter 12, Section 12.6 — an approval is an action, not a sentence.
//
// Requires a successful approvals___record_approval response for the same
// invoice within the last 24h in this policy session before a credit runs.
// The policy session id rides in the Workload Access Token across
// Gateway -> Runtime -> Gateway hops (single account and Region only).
//
// Pair with:
//   * a plain permit for approvals___record_approval, restricted to principals
//     whose user_role is account_manager (otherwise no response is recorded);
//   * credit_requires_user_principal.cedar.
// Shape follows the documented approve_claim -> disburse_payment example.
// Live-tested 2026-11-12: denies before the approval, allows after an approval for
// the same invoice in the SAME policy session, denies another invoice, and denies in
// another policy session. Cross-session approvals need durable state (Section 12.6).
// The Gateway role needs bedrock-agentcore:GetWorkloadAccessToken.

permit (
  principal is AgentCore::OAuthUser,
  action == AgentCore::Action::"refunds___issue_credit",
  resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:us-east-1:111122223333:gateway/example-gw"
)
when temporal {
  formerly within 24h AgentCore::Action::"approvals___record_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    output.invoiceId: context.input.invoice_id
  }
};
